    tailorTag: 'PER CLIENT',
    tailorTitle: 'Tailored to each client, without a new firmware',
    tailorLede: "What a unit can do is data, not code. The same firmware ships on every aircraft; what differs from one client to the next is provisioned.",
    tailor: [
      ['Behaviour packs', "The actions a unit knows ship as packs: the base set (take off, go to, scan, loiter, track, land, deliver), and payload packs for EO/IR observation, drops and radio listening. Load a client's set from the setup port, or by dropping one file on the board's USB drive. Each set is identified by its hash, and the built-in one stays as the fallback."],
      ['Capabilities per aircraft', 'Tell each unit what it carries. A mission step that requires a camera, or a drop, only goes to aircraft that have one, and zones can make exceptions per capability.'],
      ['The airframe envelope', 'Each unit knows what its aircraft can fly, and refuses, with the arithmetic, what it cannot, instead of trying and missing.'],
      ['Missions in Loom', "Your team, or your client's, describes a mission once as facts: phases, steps that wait on others, approvals, payload steps. The compiler refuses provable dead ends and the dry run plays it on the map."],
    ],
